  "verbalization": "Rituximab is associated with Non-hodgkin Lymphoma through a multi-step pathway involving the indication of Lymphoma and its subsequent link to Uracil Mustard, which in turn connects to Non-hodgkin Lymphoma. This pathway suggests a potential role of Lymphoma in the pathogenesis of Non-hodgkin Lymphoma, though the direct mechanism remains unclear. Similarly, Rituximab is also linked to Acute Lymphoblastic/lymphocytic Leukemia, which is further connected to Uracil Mustard and then to Non-hodgkin Lymphoma. These findings imply that Rituximab may exert some influence on the progression or manifestation of Non-hodgkin Lymphoma, though the precise mechanism requires further investigation. The evidence is supported by the presence of shared indications and pathways, but the exact biological process remains to be elucidated.",
